[["text","LESSON 29 / 31 • ADDITIONAL INTERVIEW TOPIC"],["heading","29. Java Collections Framework"],["text","English: Standard interfaces and implementations for lists, sets, queues and maps."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: Java වෙ9 ready-made data structures සහ ඒවොJයේ interfaces එකතුවෙක්.",395],["text","Real-world example: Application services"],["code","Collection -> List / Set / Queue"],["code","Map is a separate interface"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();\nSet<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();\nMap<Integer,String> map = new HashMap<>();\nQueue<Integer> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","Costs vary by implementation."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","Is Map a subtype of Collection?"],["text","No; Map is a separate interface."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]